  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></math>chloro<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>butadiene can undergo polymerization to form a polymer known as polychloroprene. Polychloroprene&nbsp;is a synthetic rubber commonly known as neoprene.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b3ed2d1f-3c27-4aa6-93b3-22b4b33bc44b.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 81px;\" /></p><p>Polyacrylonitrile (PAN) is an addition polymer. Addition polymers are formed through a polymerization process called addition polymerization, where monomers add to each other without the loss of any small molecules.&nbsp; Nylon-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>-nylon-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;Biodegradable polymer.&nbsp;Dacron is a type of polyester. Polyester is a polymer that belongs to the polyester family of polymers.</p><p>So, A-II; B-I; C-IV; D-III</p>",
    "image": null
